  "description": "AMUNII crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H78 Cl4 N28 O16 Yb8,2(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 3 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 3 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb1A (Yb) has 3 O neighbors; Yb2A (Yb) has 3 O neighbors; Yb3A (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb4A (Yb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.657-3.799 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.52-111.10°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H110Cl4Yb8N30O20. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies S(I).",
